205
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,912
We'll never get out now.

206
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,597
I'm tired of hiding anyway.

207
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,510
Let's fight.

208
00:11:13,593 --> 00:11:14,423
Easy there, Junior.

209
00:11:14,506 --> 00:11:16,397
You have to learn fighting's
not the only answer.

210
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:18,539
It should only be your last resort.

211
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:20,457
Let's go back this way.

212
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:22,477
We'll come out on top
near the control spire.

213
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:23,390
Good idea!

214
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:28,897
Why won't anyone listen to me?

215
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:29,810
What'd he say?

216
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,937
Hey, Davis, I almost forgot.

217
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:36,432
I saw your sister today.

218
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:38,400
Yeah? So what?

219
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:39,770
So nothing.

220
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:42,557
She probably had a lot of bad
things to say about me, didn't she?

221
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:44,380
Well, actually... I know.

222
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,757
She said that I'd bite my toenails
and spit them on the floor,

223
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,137
that I used to suck my thumb
until about a month ago,

224
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,757
that I went to bed every other Thursday.

225
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:52,297
It was laundry day, so it was all right.

226
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:54,797
Well, she talked too much, and when
I see her, I'll teach her a lesson.

227
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,997
Thanks for sharing, but she
didn't mention any of that.

228
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:57,910
Say what?

229
00:11:57,993 --> 00:11:59,697
Your sister didn't say
anything bad about you.

230
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:01,077
In fact, she didn't even mention you.

231
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,437
You're the one with the big mouth.

232
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:05,317
If you've got a problem with me,
why don't we settle it right now?

233
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:06,717
Come on, Matt, don't fight.

234
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:08,017
He's younger than you are.

235
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,688
He doesn't know any better.

236
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:12,037
I don't care how young he is.

237
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,944
He'd better learn some respect.

238
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:16,100
What does he think he is?

239
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:19,417
It's my sister, and if I want to call
her names, that's what I'm gonna do.

240
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,717
After all, that's what
brothers are here for.

241
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,140
That's enough, Davis.

242
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:28,300
I can't stand anyone who talks bad
about their brother or sister. Me?

243
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:31,320
